  <section id="platform-vision">

    <article>
      <h2>Reframing the product</h2>
      <p>My first task was to make sense of the product landscape and find the narrative that could hold everything together. Rather than treating the different products as separate entities that happened to live under the same brand, the opportunity was to reframe them as a platform — with JustRelate Home at the centre, and the Builders orbiting around it as specialised, composable capabilities.</p>
      <p>This reframing had implications beyond product design. It shaped how we talked about the platform internally and externally, how roadmaps were structured, and how teams thought about their work in relation to each other's.</p>
    </article>

    <article>
      <h2>JustRelate Home as the platform hub</h2>
      <p>JustRelate Home became the strategic centre of the platform vision — the place where all customer-facing activities converge. Marketing, Sales, and Service no longer needed to be experienced as separate silos; Home provides the unified layer that orchestrates all of them, giving users a single place to manage campaigns, customer data, pipelines, and service processes.</p>
      <p>Defining what Home should be — and equally what it shouldn't try to be — was a key part of the early work. A platform hub needs clarity of purpose to avoid becoming everything for everyone and nothing for nobody.</p>
    </article>

  </section>

  <p class="end-mark" aria-hidden="true">◼︎</p>
